  "sources_described": "The City of Milpitas delivers treated water from two wholesale sources, the San Francisco Public Utilities Commission (SFPUC, Hetch Hetchy water combined with treated local water from Calaveras and San Antonio Reservoirs via the Sunol Valley WTP) and Valley Water (Sacramento-San Joaquin Delta and local Anderson/Calero reservoir water treated at the Penitencia and Santa Teresa WTPs), both delivering treated surface water. Under normal conditions the two supplies are kept separate and not blended; an emergency groundwater well (Pinewood Well) is a backup.",
