  "violations": [
    "Page 1: 'In Calendar Year 2025, your water met all USEPA and State drinking water health standards. We are proud to report that our system had no water quality standard violations.'",
    "Page 13 (printed 11), monitoring violation: 'We are required to monitor your drinking water for specific contaminants on a regular basis. Results of regular monitoring are an indicator of whether or not your drinking water meets health standards. During May 2025, we did not complete all monitoring for coliform bacteria, and therefore, cannot be sure of the quality of your drinking water during that time.'"
  ],
  "extraction_notes": "Data tables are on PDF pages 12-13 (printed page numbers 10-11; printed page n = PDF page n+2). Table columns: 'Distribution System', 'Valley Water' (note b: fed by Santa Teresa and Penitencia WTPs) and 'SFPUC'; one entry per analyte per column that has a value, source_group = column name. Source-water rows have only Valley Water and SFPUC values; lead/copper, disinfectant residual, TTHM, HAA5 and total coliform are single distribution-system values (source_group 'Distribution System'). Where the Average cell is ND or '<x' but the Range has a numeric high, value = range high with value_basis 'range high', average null, detected true. ND, '<3', '<6', '<20', '<0.1' range-lows are recorded as 0 with the printed form in notes. MCL/AL/MRDL/ORL strings are copied as printed, including parentheses '(15)', brackets '[4]' and '1000 (NL)'. Non-regulated table has an 'ORL' column instead of MCL; it is stored in mcl_printed. Secondary and non-regulated tables have no PHG column (phg_printed null). Specific conductance unit printed 'µS/cm', stored as 'uS/cm'. pH unit printed as a dash; SFPUC pH printed '-' and omitted. Lead 90th percentile printed as 0.0025 ppb (copied exactly; possibly a units slip in the report). Turbidity primary rows: Range column holds a percent-of-time figure, not a range. Uranium note e says radioactive monitoring is every nine years (detected 2013), so sample_year is null for uranium. PDF page 10 (printed 8, 'How to Read the Water Quality Table') shows a faded, cut-off sample table whose values differ from the 2025 table (e.g. Bromate 2.45 / 2.1c, Fluoride ND / 0.4, TOC 2.5 / 1.8, Turbidity 0.28 / 0.4c) and appears to be an earlier year's layout example; those rows were NOT extracted. UCMR 5 results are stated only in text (page 9: no detections 2022-2025 for 29 PFAS plus lithium); two text-derived detected:false entries were added and flagged in notes. Individual-result exceedances inside ranges (HAA5 range high 75.0 ppb vs MCL 60; distribution turbidity range high 30 NTU vs SMCL 5; distribution odor range high 40 TON vs SMCL 3) are noted on the entries; the report declares no violations."
}